WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.978 --> 00:00:13.739
Lady Macbeth, along with all the guests, stared at her husband.

2
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.000
A murmur was spreading through the hall.

3
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.621
"Did he say ‘Banquo's ghost'?"

4
00:00:20.221 --> 00:00:20.841
whispered some.

5
00:00:21.982 --> 00:00:23.462
"He said Banquo should be dead!"

6
00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:25.803
"Who do you see, my lord?"

7
00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:27.303
Ross asked the king.

8
00:00:28.123 --> 00:00:29.684
But Lady Macbeth quickly interrupted.

9
00:00:30.432 --> 00:00:33.913
"Please, such questions will only worsen his condition."

10
00:00:35.193 --> 00:00:40.935
Then, turning to all the guests she said, "I'm sorry that our evening has been spoiled," and she

11
00:00:40.995 --> 00:00:42.875
wished them all a kind goodnight.

12
00:00:43.836 --> 00:00:47.457
Attendants ushered the guests out of the hall, leaving Macbeth and his wife alone.

13
00:00:47.477 --> 00:00:52.358
"The ghost is gone; I am myself again," he reassured her.

14
00:00:52.378 --> 00:00:53.378
"Is it late?"

15
00:00:54.498 --> 00:00:56.519
Quietly, they began to talk about the evening.

16
00:00:57.499 --> 00:01:00.280
Lady Macbeth pointed out that Macduff had been absent.

17
00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.761
"He refused our invitation," she said.

18
00:01:03.781 --> 00:01:07.602
"It makes me suspect him," agreed Macbeth.

19
00:01:08.462 --> 00:01:13.484
Macbeth kept spies in the houses of all the Scottish noblemen, but he trusted Macduff the least.

20
00:01:14.524 --> 00:01:17.905
The more they talked, the more fears and suspicions grew in his mind.

21
00:01:18.785 --> 00:01:23.426
Before he and Lady Macbeth went to bed, he resolved to visit the three witches once again.

22
00:01:23.446 --> 00:01:28.688
"I must know the worst," he said, "even by the worst means."

23
00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:33.319
The witches, of course, knew that Macbeth was coming long before he arrived.

24
00:01:34.199 --> 00:01:37.462
In their dark cave, a huge cauldron bubbled over a fire.

25
00:01:38.002 --> 00:01:45.027
They circled around it, chanting: Round about the cauldron go; into it, poisoned entrails throw.

26
00:01:45.888 --> 00:01:52.292
Eye of newt and toe of frog, wool of bat and tongue of dog, Baboon's blood and tail

27
00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:55.074
of snake, in the cauldron boil and bake.

28
00:01:55.675 --> 00:01:59.786
Double, double, toil and trouble; fire burn and cauldron bubble!

29
00:02:00.866 --> 00:02:04.349
Then, using a thick bone, they stirred the stinking pot together.

30
00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:10.614
Near the heath where he first saw the witches, a day's journey from the palace, Macbeth found the

31
00:02:10.715 --> 00:02:11.735
entrance to their cave.

32
00:02:12.716 --> 00:02:14.938
A foul smell wafted from the dark opening.

33
00:02:15.859 --> 00:02:20.362
He covered his nose with a corner of his cloak and, ducking his head, stepped inside.

34
00:02:21.263 --> 00:02:25.807
An oily smoke burned his eyes, but he could see the three ugly witches in the red light

35
00:02:25.847 --> 00:02:26.808
of the cauldron's fire.

36
00:02:27.604 --> 00:02:30.245
"What is it you do, you black and unholy hags?"

37
00:02:30.845 --> 00:02:31.286
he asked.

38
00:02:31.306 --> 00:02:36.608
"A deed without a name," said the first witch with a crooked smile.

39
00:02:36.628 --> 00:02:39.589
"Come!" commanded the second witch.

40
00:02:40.249 --> 00:02:42.730
"We'll answer you," said the third.

41
00:02:43.591 --> 00:02:49.473
Macbeth stepped closer and watched as the last witch dropped something red and wriggling into the bubbling liquid.

42
00:02:50.353 --> 00:02:54.635
A dark smoke rose, and Macbeth saw a ghostly head materialize in the air.

43
00:02:55.816 --> 00:02:58.085
It wore a helmet, as if armed for war.

44
00:02:58.105 --> 00:03:04.169
"Tell me, you unknown power―" Macbeth began, but the first witch interrupted him.

45
00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:05.771
"He knows your thoughts.

46
00:03:06.351 --> 00:03:07.792
Listen and speak not."

47
00:03:07.812 --> 00:03:10.994
"Macbeth! Macbeth!

48
00:03:11.495 --> 00:03:13.236
Beware Macduff!"

49
00:03:13.976 --> 00:03:14.537
said the vision.

50
00:03:14.557 --> 00:03:18.780
"It knows my fear and cautions me well," said Macbeth.

51
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:24.164
"Just one word more—" but before he could ask, the vision descended into the pot.

52
00:03:25.128 --> 00:03:27.130
A second apparition rose from the cauldron.

53
00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:29.772
This one was in the form of a bloody child.

54
00:03:29.792 --> 00:03:32.474
"Macbeth! Macbeth!

55
00:03:33.055 --> 00:03:39.860
Laugh and scorn the power of men," it said, "for none born of woman shall harm Macbeth."

56
00:03:40.841 --> 00:03:42.943
Then it too descended into the creeping vapors.

57
00:03:43.964 --> 00:03:44.924
A third vision rose.

58
00:03:45.545 --> 00:03:49.208
This time it was a child wearing a crown and carrying a branch in its hand.

59
00:03:50.209 --> 00:03:53.852
It spoke: "Take no care, whoever your enemies are.

60
00:03:54.580 --> 00:04:00.223
Macbeth shall never be defeated until great Birnam Wood comes to high Dunsinane Hill."

61
00:04:00.243 --> 00:04:02.303
"That will never be!"

62
00:04:03.104 --> 00:04:04.564
Macbeth whispered excitedly.

63
00:04:04.584 --> 00:04:08.906
"How can the trees pull up their roots and march against my castle there?

64
00:04:09.867 --> 00:04:11.647
And ‘none born of woman' shall harm me?

65
00:04:12.048 --> 00:04:17.830
Then, Macduff, I have no reason to fear you But just in case, you will not live."

66
00:04:19.271 --> 00:04:21.992
He turned to look back at the cauldron, but the witches were gone.

67
00:04:22.732 --> 00:04:25.513
The fire was out and the cave was suddenly cold and desolate.

68
00:04:26.514 --> 00:04:28.174
Outside, the air was damp and fresh.

69
00:04:28.795 --> 00:04:32.956
Feeling as if he had awakened from a drugged sleep, Macbeth inhaled deeply.

70
00:04:33.757 --> 00:04:36.418
On the long journey back to the palace, his thoughts churned.

71
00:04:36.438 --> 00:04:40.759
"They are the devil's sisters, I'm sure, but they make me bold!

72
00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:45.441
From now on, the first thought of my heart will be the first act of my hand!

73
00:04:46.242 --> 00:04:50.804
I have waded so deep into a river of blood that to go back is just as far

74
00:04:50.864 --> 00:04:51.604
as to go on."

75
00:04:52.448 --> 00:04:53.389
His face grew grim.

76
00:04:53.409 --> 00:04:56.090
"‘Beware Macduff,' they warned me.

77
00:04:56.691 --> 00:04:58.031
I must act on this advice!"

78
00:04:59.392 --> 00:05:02.214
When he arrived at the palace, a messenger was waiting for him.

79
00:05:03.134 --> 00:05:07.317
It was his spy from Macduff's castle with news that Macduff had fled to England.

80
00:05:08.417 --> 00:05:09.618
Macbeth clenched his fists.

81
00:05:09.638 --> 00:05:11.819
"He has anticipated my plan!"

82
00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:18.603
In England, Duncan's oldest son, Malcolm, had taken refuge at the court of the king, where many were

83
00:05:18.643 --> 00:05:19.744
sympathetic to his cause.

84
00:05:20.808 --> 00:05:25.370
Since the day Macbeth had come to power, the news from Scotland had grown steadily worse.

85
00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:27.791
The Scottish nobles feared him.

86
00:05:28.231 --> 00:05:31.152
And anyone who Macbeth suspected lived in terror of his army.

87
00:05:32.173 --> 00:05:34.034
Rumors of Macbeth's murders were spreading.

88
00:05:34.594 --> 00:05:36.335
People whispered to each other about war.

89
00:05:37.195 --> 00:05:41.217
With the help of the English lords, Malcolm was slowly gathering an army of his own.

90
00:05:42.197 --> 00:05:46.339
The king of England had offered him ten thousand men, and more were joining every day.

91
00:05:47.339 --> 00:05:51.918
When Macduff arrived at the English court, he immediately offered to help the young prince take back his

92
00:05:51.978 --> 00:05:52.719
father's throne.

93
00:05:52.739 --> 00:05:59.405
"Macbeth is a tyrant," said Macduff, as he strolled with Malcolm outside the English court.

94
00:05:59.425 --> 00:06:03.908
"Every morning, new widows mourn and new orphans cry.

95
00:06:04.389 --> 00:06:06.751
Scotland suffers badly under his rule."

96
00:06:07.592 --> 00:06:10.294
"Others hear our country's cry," said Malcolm.

97
00:06:10.314 --> 00:06:14.257
"The English lords Siward and Northumberland have come to our side."

98
00:06:15.238 --> 00:06:20.473
Just then, a man approached from across the lawn, and they quickly recognized Ross, their fellow countryman.

99
00:06:21.354 --> 00:06:25.675
After they greeted each other, Macduff asked, "How do things stand in Scotland?"

100
00:06:26.476 --> 00:06:27.296
Ross shook his head.

101
00:06:27.316 --> 00:06:30.057
"Our homeland is becoming a graveyard.

102
00:06:30.477 --> 00:06:32.318
There are new atrocities every day."

103
00:06:32.338 --> 00:06:34.279
"How are my wife and children?"

104
00:06:34.899 --> 00:06:35.499
asked Macduff.

105
00:06:35.519 --> 00:06:38.020
"Macbeth has not assaulted their peace?"

106
00:06:39.001 --> 00:06:39.841
Ross paused.

107
00:06:39.861 --> 00:06:44.003
"I have words that I would rather howl in the desert than tell you.

108
00:06:44.903 --> 00:06:49.634
Fife Castle has been attacked, and your wife and children savagely slaughtered."

109
00:06:50.555 --> 00:06:51.436
"Merciful heaven!"

110
00:06:52.376 --> 00:06:55.659
exclaimed Malcolm, but Macduff was stunned and silent.

111
00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:57.781
There was a pause.

112
00:06:58.641 --> 00:06:59.582
"What, man!

113
00:07:00.143 --> 00:07:02.665
Give words to your grief," said Malcolm.

114
00:07:02.685 --> 00:07:04.286
"My children?"

115
00:07:05.187 --> 00:07:05.787
asked Macduff.

116
00:07:05.807 --> 00:07:12.332
"Wife, children, servants—all that Macbeth's murderers found," said Ross.

117
00:07:12.352 --> 00:07:15.114
"Oh, torment and hell!

118
00:07:15.535 --> 00:07:17.484
My wife killed too?"

119
00:07:17.504 --> 00:07:18.125
cried Macduff.

120
00:07:18.885 --> 00:07:19.886
Ross nodded solemnly.

121
00:07:19.906 --> 00:07:21.707
"My children!

122
00:07:22.167 --> 00:07:22.607
Not all?

123
00:07:22.888 --> 00:07:23.868
Please, not all!"

124
00:07:23.888 --> 00:07:27.351
"You must bear it like a man," said Malcolm.

125
00:07:28.311 --> 00:07:29.792
Macduff turned to him angrily.

126
00:07:29.812 --> 00:07:31.693
"I shall do so!

127
00:07:32.174 --> 00:07:33.695
But I must feel it as a man, too.

128
00:07:34.275 --> 00:07:37.898
There was never anything so precious to me as my sweet family.

129
00:07:38.478 --> 00:07:41.660
Gone!" He turned from them and strode away.

130
00:07:42.321 --> 00:07:43.041
Then he turned back.

131
00:07:43.061 --> 00:07:47.284
"This grief is a whetstone to sharpen my sword!"

132
00:07:47.916 --> 00:07:48.316
he said.

133
00:07:48.336 --> 00:07:51.599
"I won't let this sadness blunt my heart.

134
00:07:52.479 --> 00:07:56.442
Oh, I could fill my eyes with tears and cry sorrows with my tongue.

135
00:07:57.062 --> 00:07:57.523
But enough!

136
00:07:58.283 --> 00:08:03.567
Bring this demon of Scotland face to face with me, set him within reach of my sword, and

137
00:08:03.627 --> 00:08:05.909
heaven forgive me if he escapes death!"
